{
  "note": "✍️ The keyboard and clipboard editing law of a focused text field every renderer shares: caret motion by character, word (Alt: to the word end; Ctrl: to the next word start; both back to the previous word start), line (Meta, Home, End) and text (Ctrl+Home/End), vertical motion across logical lines keeping the column in scalars, selection by Shift, word and line deletion, select-all, copy and cut. Offsets are UTF-8 bytes; `anchor == caret` is no selection. A word is a run of letters, digits and `_`, a run of other marks, or a blank run; blanks are skipped before a word. A single-line field turns pasted line breaks into one blank. Rust `route_edit_key`; TypeScript twin judges the word motions with `Intl.Segmenter`.",
